        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most houses, the best outage generator is a dual fuel portable in the 7,000 to 9,500 running watt range connected through an interlock or transfer switch, with a fuel plan for three days. If your outages are long, frequent or dangerous to the people in your home, a Generac Guardian 22kW standby unit is the investment that ends the problem.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, two rules do not bend: the engine runs outside, well away from the house with battery CO alarms inside, and it never connects to your wiring except through a proper transfer switch or interlock. Get those right and every machine on this list will do its job.
